{"route":"/docs/6.0/helpers/stretched-link/","version":"6.0","renderedVersion":"6.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Stretched link","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Make any HTML element or Bootstrap component clickable by “stretching” a nested link via CSS."},"blocks":[{"id":"content--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Add <code>.stretched-link</code> to a link to make its <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Containing_block\">containing block</a> clickable via a <code>::after</code> pseudo element. In most cases, this means that an element with <code>position: relative;</code> that contains a link with the <code>.stretched-link</code> class is clickable. Please note given <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS21/visuren.html#propdef-position\">how CSS <code>position</code> works</a>, <code>.stretched-link</code> cannot be mixed with most table elements."},{"id":"content--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Cards have <code>position: relative</code> by default in Bootstrap, so in this case you can safely add the <code>.stretched-link</code> class to a link in the card without any other HTML changes."},{"id":"content--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Multiple links and tap targets are not recommended with stretched links. However, some <code>position</code> and <code>z-index</code> styles can help should this be required."},{"id":"content--example-1","type":"demo","key":"4e06a659d3a31f1d47d7","height":300},{"id":"content--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"card\" style=\"width: 18rem;\">\n  <img src=\"...\" class=\"card-img-top\" alt=\"...\">\n  <div class=\"card-body\">\n    <h5 class=\"card-title\">Card with stretched link</h5>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">Some quick example text to build on the card title and make up the bulk of the card’s content.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"btn-solid theme-primary stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":""},{"id":"content--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Most custom components do not have <code>position: relative</code> by default, so we need to add the <code>.position-relative</code> here to prevent the link from stretching outside the parent element."},{"id":"content--example-2","type":"demo","key":"3f922185e4deb3997646","height":147},{"id":"content--code-2","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"d-flex position-relative\">\n  <img src=\"...\" class=\"flex-shrink-0 me-3\" alt=\"...\">\n  <div>\n    <h5 class=\"mt-0\">Custom component with stretched link</h5>\n    <p>This is some placeholder content for the custom component. It is intended to mimic what some real-world content would look like, and we’re using it here to give the component a bit of body and size.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":""},{"id":"content--example-3","type":"demo","key":"d36d8cdf30beb1315d40","height":147},{"id":"content--code-3","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"row g-0 bg-1 position-relative\">\n  <div class=\"md:col-6 md:mb-0 md:p-4\">\n    <img src=\"...\" class=\"w-100\" alt=\"...\">\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"md:col-6 p-4 md:ps-0\">\n    <h5 class=\"mt-0\">Columns with stretched link</h5>\n    <p>Another instance of placeholder content for this other custom component. It is intended to mimic what some real-world content would look like, and we’re using it here to give the component a bit of body and size.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":""},{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block","type":"heading","en":"Identifying the containing block","level":2},{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"If the stretched link doesn’t seem to work, the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Containing_block#Identifying_the_containing_block\">containing block</a> will probably be the cause. The following CSS properties will make an element the containing block:"},{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--item-1","type":"item","en":"A <code>position</code> value other than <code>static</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--item-2","type":"item","en":"A <code>transform</code> or <code>perspective</code> value other than <code>none</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--item-3","type":"item","en":"A <code>will-change</code> value of <code>transform</code> or <code>perspective</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--item-4","type":"item","en":"A <code>filter</code> value other than <code>none</code> or a <code>will-change</code> value of <code>filter</code> (only works on Firefox)"}]}]},{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--example-1","type":"demo","key":"c6a58cf7f6015a0b0921","height":300},{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"card\" style=\"width: 18rem;\">\n  <img src=\"...\" class=\"card-img-top\" alt=\"...\">\n  <div class=\"card-body\">\n    <h5 class=\"card-title\">Card with stretched links</h5>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">Some quick example text to build on the card title and make up the bulk of the card’s content.</p>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">\n      <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link fg-danger\" style=\"position: relative;\">Stretched link will not work here, because <code>position: relative</code> is added to the link</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"card-text bg-1\" style=\"transform: rotate(0);\">\n      This <a href=\"#\" class=\"fg-warning stretched-link\">stretched link</a> will only be spread over the <code>p</code>-tag, because a transform is applied to it.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":""},{"id":"css","type":"heading","en":"CSS","level":2},{"id":"variables","type":"heading","en":"Variables","level":3},{"id":"variables--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Stretched links use local CSS variables on <code>.stretched-link</code> for real-time customization. Values for the CSS variables are generated from Sass maps unique to each component and applied to the aforementioned class."},{"id":"variables--code-1","type":"code","value":"// stylelint-disable-next-line scss/dollar-variable-default\n$stretched-link-tokens: defaults(\n  (\n    --stretched-link-z-index: 1,\n  ),\n  $stretched-link-tokens\n);","language":""},{"id":"sass-variable","type":"heading","en":"Sass variable","level":3},{"id":"sass-variable--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The pseudo-element used to stretch the link defaults to <code>after</code> and can be changed via the <code>$stretched-link-pseudo-element</code> Sass variable. This can’t be a CSS variable since it’s compiled directly into the generated selector."},{"id":"sass-variable--code-1","type":"code","value":"$stretched-link-pseudo-element: after;","language":""}],"demos":[{"key":"4e06a659d3a31f1d47d7","html":"<div class=\"card\" style=\"width: 18rem;\">\n  <svg aria-label=\"Card image cap\" class=\"bd-placeholder-img card-img-top\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\" role=\"img\" width=\"100%\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><title>Card image cap</title><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"var(--bs-bg-2)\"></rect></svg>\n  <div class=\"card-body\">\n    <h5 class=\"card-title\">Card with stretched link</h5>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">Some quick example text to build on the card title and make up the bulk of the card’s content.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"btn-solid theme-primary stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"3f922185e4deb3997646","html":"<div class=\"d-flex position-relative\">\n  <svg aria-label=\"Generic placeholder image\" class=\"bd-placeholder-img flex-shrink-0 me-3\" height=\"144\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\" role=\"img\" width=\"144\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><title>Generic placeholder image</title><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"var(--bs-bg-2)\"></rect></svg>\n  <div>\n    <h5 class=\"mt-0\">Custom component with stretched link</h5>\n    <p>This is some placeholder content for the custom component. It is intended to mimic what some real-world content would look like, and we’re using it here to give the component a bit of body and size.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"d36d8cdf30beb1315d40","html":"<div class=\"row g-0 bg-1 position-relative\">\n  <div class=\"md:col-6 md:mb-0 md:p-4\">\n    <svg aria-label=\"Generic placeholder image\" class=\"bd-placeholder-img w-100\" height=\"200\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\" role=\"img\" width=\"100%\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><title>Generic placeholder image</title><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"var(--bs-bg-2)\"></rect></svg>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"md:col-6 p-4 md:ps-0\">\n    <h5 class=\"mt-0\">Columns with stretched link</h5>\n    <p>Another instance of placeholder content for this other custom component. It is intended to mimic what some real-world content would look like, and we’re using it here to give the component a bit of body and size.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"c6a58cf7f6015a0b0921","html":"<div class=\"card\" style=\"width: 18rem;\">\n  <svg aria-label=\"Card image cap\" class=\"bd-placeholder-img card-img-top\" height=\"180\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\" role=\"img\" width=\"100%\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><title>Card image cap</title><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"var(--bs-bg-2)\"></rect></svg>\n  <div class=\"card-body\">\n    <h5 class=\"card-title\">Card with stretched links</h5>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">Some quick example text to build on the card title and make up the bulk of the card’s content.</p>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">\n      <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link fg-danger\" style=\"position: relative;\">Stretched link will not work here, because <code>position: relative</code> is added to the link</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"card-text bg-1\" style=\"transform: rotate(0);\">\n      This <a href=\"#\" class=\"fg-warning stretched-link\">stretched link</a> will only be spread over the <code>p</code>-tag, because a transform is applied to it.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Install","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/install"},{"en":"AI","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/ai"},{"en":"Approach","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/approach"},{"en":"CSS variables","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/css-variables"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/javascript"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/browsers-devices"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/accessibility"},{"en":"Quickstart","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/quickstart"},{"en":"npm","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/npm"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/webpack"},{"en":"Parcel","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/parcel"},{"en":"Vite","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/vite"},{"en":"Contribute","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/contribute"},{"en":"Migration","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/migration"},{"en":"Overview","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/customize/overview"},{"en":"Sass","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/customize/sass"},{"en":"Options","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/customize/opt